mes down and {w} times across.\")\n    for ty in range(h):\n        for tx in range(w):\n            out[ty*h:(ty+1)*h, tx*w:(tx+1)*w] = g\n        emit(out, f\"Stamp {w} copies of the input across tile row {ty + 1} of {h}.\")\n    emit(out, \"Final grid: the input tiled in an input-sized grid of copies.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"rigid":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- No tile is recoloured, mirrored or masked."}],"repeat":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- The content confirms plain tiling."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"Stamp the input into each tile position, one band of tiles at a time."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Allocate a 9x9 canvas: the 3x3 input will be tiled 3 times down and 3 times across."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Stamp the input into each tile position, one band of tiles at a time."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamp 3 copies of the input across tile row 1 of 3."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Stamp 3 copies of the input across tile row 2 of 3."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- The output size is always the input size squared:"},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Allocate a 9x9 canvas: the 3x3 input will be tiled 3 times down and 3 times across."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Allocate a 4x4 canvas: the 2x2 input will be tiled 2 times down and 2 times across."}],"scale":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"So the scale factor equals the input's side length."}],"assembly":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"- The content confirms plain tiling."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"ddb0a4732a0911bb177f1b0a90c074bb55ce8b60a27c3d95ad7cc2f9902c517c","task_sha256":"c8e5771e3b885f734eae61d2452b8dbda3b775d64d3eb6435df82e014eeb8179","validation":"Frozen corpus recorded successful replay on teaching fixtures; synth